<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    angr-inspired duplicate-declaration collapse (option dedupvardecls).

    Source: angr testcase test_decompiling_x8664_cvs :: main (binary
    binaries/tests/x86_64/cvs, x86-64, gcc).  angr's variable recovery yields
    exactly one variable per storage location, so its declaration block lists
    each local once.  kuna's C printer instead walks HighVariables (the W4
    ScopeLocal Symbol walk is the missing surface), so when the angr-style
    naming maps many distinct scalar HighVariables that share one stack slot to
    the SAME name + type + storage, kuna emits one declaration line PER HIGH: a
    wall of textually identical declarations.  The function body refers to all of
    them by the one shared name, so the duplicate declaration LINES are pure noise
    (and, strictly, invalid C re-declarations).

    On the full (debug-info) binary the slot 'stack - 0x3c' (option_index) is
    declared 166 times and 'stack - 0x58' (v19) 53 / 3 times, blowing main up to
    ~680 loc vs angr's ~472 (see docs/features/x8664-cvs-863633).  This isolated
    chunk has no debug info and recovers fewer highs, so the duplication is
    milder but identical in kind: slot 'stack - 0x58' is declared 4 times.

    Stage model: S9 (Surface Rendering), PrintC::emit_local_var_decls, the
    local-declaration symbol-vs-high walk (naming-policy sub-stage).  kuna already
    collapses this for COMPOSITE (array/struct/union) mapped symbols; this is the
    scalar analogue, gated so default output is byte-identical.

    The collapse suppresses a declaration ONLY when its fully-rendered signature
    (type + name + array adornment + storage comment) is byte-identical to one
    already emitted: provably lossless, and the body markup is unchanged.

    Assertions are on the name-independent storage comment '; // stack - 0xNN'
    (one per declaration of that slot), summed over both passes:
      Pass 1 (option dedupvardecls off): slot 0x58 declared 4x, slot 0x3c 1x
        - the bug (duplicate scalar declarations); 0x58 still shows it.
      Pass 2 (option dedupvardecls on): each slot declared exactly 1x - the fix.
    So slot 0x58 totals 4 + 1 = 5 and slot 0x3c totals 1 + 1 = 2.  A broken fix
    (no collapse: 8 / >=3) or an over-eager collapse (under 5 / under 2) fails.
    (kuna: since the addr-tied merge coalescing fix (VariablePiece grouping no longer
    aborts on a reused stack slot), the OFF pass already coalesces 0x3c to 1x, so its
    total dropped from 3 to 2; dedupvardecls is still exercised by the 0x58 case.)
    (kuna GH-181: the snipReads INDIRECT carve-out places cover-trim COPYs after
    the effect-causing call, so the S6 merge now coalesces the reused 0x58 slot
    too: both slots are 1x in the OFF pass and each totals 1 + 1 = 2.  The
    collapse feature itself is exercised by ghdec-symbol-keyed-local-decls,
    whose OFF pass still produces a genuine duplicate declaration.)

    Chunks: cvs main's .text bytes from 0x404df0 (plus slack so the jump-table
    over-read decodes), and the getopt-dispatch table in .rodata at 0x49b8f0.
    External calls/globals are unmapped and render as sub_/dat_; only main is
    decompiled.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x404df0">

</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x49b8f0">

</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x404df0" name="main"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <!-- kuna: stackguard is now default-on (DIV-14) and strips the -fstack-protector canary epilogue in this cvs main, changing the 0x3c decl count. It is not the flag under test here, so keep it off for both passes (the off-baseline these dedupvardecls assertions were pinned against). -->
  <com>option stackguard off</com>
  <com>option dedupvardecls off</com>
  <com>lo fu main</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option dedupvardecls on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="angr-dedupvardecls #1: slot 0x58 declared 1x (off, now merge-coalesced per GH-181) + 1x (on) = 2 total" min="2" max="2">; // stack - 0x58</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="angr-dedupvardecls #2: slot 0x3c declared 1x (off, now merge-coalesced) + 1x (on) = 2 total" min="2" max="2">; // stack - 0x3c</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
